course: dictionary
lesson: 5171
title: Names in context
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words are names of people or places, and they always start with a capital letter. «In Kirkcaldy, Granny takes Islay to the chippy» shows Islay as a girl's name, because Granny is taking her somewhere.
explain: Islay is also a place: an island off the west coast of Scotland. The clues are in the words around it, such as island and Scotland. When you meet a capital letter in the middle of a sentence, ask yourself: is this a person, a place or a thing?
explain: «Dinnae tell yer mam we had chips again» is Scots. Dinnae means don't, and the sentence tells you what it means. Context helps you work out words from other places, and a dictionary settles it when you are unsure.
fact: Islay is a proper noun, so it starts with a capital letter.
fact: Islay is an island off the west coast of Scotland, in the Inner Hebrides.
fact: Islay is famous for whisky distilleries, peat, birds and wild geese.
fact: Islay is said EYE-luh, not iss-lay.
fact: Islay can also be a person's name, as in «Granny takes Islay to the chippy».
exercise: «In Kirkcaldy, Granny takes Islay to the chippy.» In this sentence, what is Islay? | An island off Scotland | A chip shop | *A girl's name | A type of whisky
exercise: Islay is an island off the west coast of which country? | *Scotland | Australia | Wales | England
exercise: How is the word Islay said? | iss-lay | eye-LAY | *EYE-luh | ISS-lee
test: Islay is famous for which drink? | Milk | Lemonade | *Whisky | Tea
test: Which word is a name and needs a capital letter? | island | birds | *Islay | peat
exam: Islay is part of which group of islands? | The Faroe Islands | *The Inner Hebrides | The Balearic Islands | The Canary Islands
